sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: DECISIONS R1 (no Node, no run), root-of-trust-gateway-only (App JWT stays in the Gateway). docs/reference/github-app.md.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: github:app:sync
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>App installations
  CLI->>GW: github:app:sync<br/>--json
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit github:app:sync`
  %%> - syntax: `[--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - nothing; it refreshes the Gateway's one App
  %%> When:
  %%> - after you install the App on an account or change its repositories
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - `--idempotency-key`: the refresh answers at once and is safe to repeat
  Note over GW: Check the App<br/>sign App JWT · 9 min
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the Gateway
  %%> - the Gateway has a registered App, else `github.app_missing`
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - signs a short App JWT with the App key; the key and the JWT never leave the Gateway
  %%> Why no Swamp run:
  %%> - it touches no Node (R1), and App-level authority stays in the Gateway
  GW->>GH: List installations<br/>GET /app/installations
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - asks GitHub for every installation of the App, with the JWT
  %%> - answers within the request; no queue job, no task to follow
  alt GitHub answers
    GH-->>GW: 2 installations
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - per installation: the account, `user` or `organization`, `all` or `selected` repositories, and whether it is suspended
    Note over GW: Store the observation<br/>current · observed_at
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the installation list is stored with `installations_status: current` and the time
    %%> - an Activity entry records the refresh
    GW-->>CLI: App and installations<br/>same as github:app:show
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the App and one row per installation, at once
  else GitHub fails
    GH--xGW: refused or no reply
    %%> When:
    %%> - GitHub cannot be reached, or refuses the JWT
    Note over GW: Keep the last list<br/>github.unavailable
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the last stored list stays, with its `observed_at`; it becomes `stale` after five minutes
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again
    GW-->>CLI: github.unavailable<br/>last list · stale
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the error and the last known list, at once
  end
